              "name": "runner",
              "externalId": "2"
            },
            "kind": "issue",
            "number": "1788"
          },
          "id": "106331"
        },
        "body": "Unfortunately, https://v18.next.forgejo.org/franke/forgejo-runner-premature-success-repro/src/commit/9d2c3c495e41bb0e6d4aaa111447e793de050ad1/exec_stream_closed_test.go doesn't reproduce the problem, because it mocks the Docker API in Go.\r\n\r\nThis workflow should do it:\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\non:\r\n  workflow_dispatch:\r\njobs:\r\n  test:\r\n    runs-on: debian\r\n    steps:\r\n      - run: |\r\n          apt-get update && apt-get install -y python3\r\n      - run: |\r\n          import os\r\n          import time\r\n          import sys\r\n        \r\n          os.close(sys.stdout.fileno())\r\n          \r\n          time.sleep(10)\r\n        shell:\r\n          python3\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe step is marked as succeeded after 0s instead of 10s.\r\n\r\nhttps://code.forgejo.org/forgejo/runner/src/commit/c07a9b3669dc64d498273d47ce0e6974718792f1/act/container/docker/run.go#L766\r\n\r\ncontinues until it encounters an EOF. Afterwards, Docker's `execInspect` is invoked.\r\n\r\nhttps://code.forgejo.org/forgejo/runner/src/commit/c07a9b3669dc64d498273d47ce0e6974718792f1/act/container/docker/run.go#L771\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, it doesn't seem to help us much. It immediately returns `Running` as `false`, and the exit code is always 0, even if there's none, because Go.\r\n\r\nThe same script invoked using `podman exec <container> python3 test.py` takes ~10s.\r\n\r\nEither, the workflow doesn't reproduce the problem perfectly, or `podman exec` does something differently. If somebody has any ideas, please let me know.\r\n"
      },
